# 32-bit (abi_x86_32) builds of the libraries Steam needs.
#
# games-util/steam-launcher (steam-overlay) requires a 32-bit fontconfig,
# Mesa, libdrm, libpulse, Vulkan loader and libudev, and each of those needs
# its own dependencies as 32-bit too.  This is that whole set and nothing
# more: enabling abi_x86_32 for every package instead would rebuild several
# hundred libraries, three LLVM/Clang slots among them, for no benefit.
#
# The binhost builds these packages with this file in place.  A machine
# needs the same file to get binaries for them, whether it runs Steam or
# not; without it, it compiles these packages itself.
#
# Generated, do not edit by hand.  The roots are in
# packages/tiers/25-steam-runtime.txt; when Gentoo adds a dependency, that
# tier stops resolving, the build reports it, and the file is regenerated
# with scripts/use-closure.sh (see docs/STEAM.md).
